      "notes": "Page 19 also recommends ceramic without specifying dielectric; three 22 uF ceramic capacitors suitable for most applications, not a guaranteed minimum. Select COUT for ripple/transients and allow voltage derating. External series R-C compensation from COMP to AGND is required (p3); p20 gives FP1=1/(2*pi*RLOAD*COUT), FZ1=1/(2*pi*RCOMP*CCOMP). In CCM, FRHPZ=RLOAD/(2*pi*L)*(VIN/VOUT)^2 (p21), worst at minimum VIN and maximum output power. Page 23 example: RCOMP=24.9 kohm, CCOMP=3.3 nF for VIN 3\u201310 V, VOUT 12 V, 2 A. No universal output current rating: limited by allowable temperature rise, current limit and VIN (p21). Switch current limit is NOT output current; p6 gives 19/25/29 A min/typ/max at TJ=25 C, GATE=GND, duty=40%."
